# Testing & Debugging Rules

## Code Quality & Debugging

### Console Logging Standards
- **Descriptive Messages**: Use clear, descriptive console messages for debugging
- **Log Levels**: Use appropriate log levels (log, warn, error, info, debug)
- **Structured Logging**: Log objects and arrays in a readable format
- **Production Removal**: Remove or disable debug logs in production

### Error Handling
- **Try-Catch Blocks**: Wrap all async operations and API calls in try-catch blocks
- **Error Messages**: Provide clear, actionable error messages for users
- **Error Recovery**: Implement graceful fallbacks when operations fail
- **Error Logging**: Log errors with sufficient context for debugging

### Code Comments
- **Complex Logic**: Comment complex business logic and algorithms
- **Non-Obvious Code**: Explain code that isn't immediately clear
- **Business Rules**: Document business rules and requirements
- **TODO Comments**: Use TODO comments for future improvements

### Documentation Standards
- **Function Documentation**: Document all public functions with JSDoc comments
- **Parameter Documentation**: Document parameter types, constraints, and examples
- **Return Value Documentation**: Document return values and their types
- **Usage Examples**: Provide usage examples for complex functions

## Browser Compatibility & Testing

### Cross-Browser Testing
- **Feature Detection**: Use feature detection instead of browser detection
- **Progressive Enhancement**: Ensure core functionality works without JavaScript
- **Fallback Handling**: Provide alternatives when features aren't supported
- **Testing Matrix**: Test across major browsers (Chrome, Firefox, Safari, Edge)

### Mobile Testing
- **Responsive Testing**: Test responsive design across different screen sizes
- **Touch Testing**: Test touch interactions and gestures
- **Performance Testing**: Test performance on mobile devices
- **Accessibility Testing**: Ensure mobile accessibility compliance

### Performance Testing
- **Load Time Testing**: Monitor page load times and performance metrics
- **Memory Testing**: Check for memory leaks and excessive memory usage
- **Network Testing**: Test performance under different network conditions
- **User Experience Testing**: Test actual user interactions and workflows

## Error Tracking & Monitoring

### Error Monitoring
- **Error Tracking**: Implement comprehensive error tracking and logging
- **User Feedback**: Collect user feedback on errors and issues
- **Performance Monitoring**: Monitor application performance and bottlenecks
- **Alerting**: Set up alerts for critical errors and performance issues

### Debugging Tools
- **Browser DevTools**: Use browser developer tools for debugging
- **Network Monitoring**: Monitor network requests and responses
- **Performance Profiling**: Use performance profiling tools to identify bottlenecks
- **Memory Profiling**: Use memory profiling to identify memory leaks

## Testing Standards

### Unit Testing
- **Test Coverage**: Maintain high test coverage for critical functionality
- **Test Organization**: Organize tests to mirror source code structure
- **Test Naming**: Use descriptive test names that indicate what is being tested
- **Test Data**: Use realistic test data and fixtures

### Integration Testing
- **API Testing**: Test API integrations and data flow
- **Component Testing**: Test component interactions and integrations
- **End-to-End Testing**: Test complete user workflows
- **Regression Testing**: Ensure new changes don't break existing functionality

### Manual Testing
- **User Acceptance Testing**: Test from the user's perspective
- **Edge Case Testing**: Test edge cases and error conditions
- **Accessibility Testing**: Test accessibility compliance
- **Usability Testing**: Test user experience and interface usability

## Quality Assurance

### Code Review Process
- **Review Checklist**: Use consistent code review checklists
- **Testing Verification**: Ensure tests are written for new functionality
- **Documentation Review**: Verify documentation is updated with code changes
- **Performance Review**: Review code for performance implications

### Continuous Improvement
- **Feedback Loop**: Establish feedback loops for continuous improvement
- **Metrics Tracking**: Track quality metrics and improvement over time
- **Best Practices**: Continuously update and follow best practices
- **Team Training**: Provide training on testing and debugging practices

## Debugging Workflow

### Problem Identification
- **Reproduce Issues**: Ensure issues can be consistently reproduced
- **Isolate Problems**: Isolate problems to specific components or functions
- **Root Cause Analysis**: Identify root causes of issues
- **Impact Assessment**: Assess the impact of issues on users

### Solution Development
- **Incremental Fixes**: Make incremental fixes and test each change
- **Regression Testing**: Ensure fixes don't introduce new issues
- **Documentation Updates**: Update documentation with fixes and changes
- **User Communication**: Communicate fixes and improvements to users

### Prevention Strategies
- **Code Reviews**: Use code reviews to catch issues early
- **Automated Testing**: Implement automated testing to prevent regressions
- **Monitoring**: Use monitoring to detect issues before users report them
- **Best Practices**: Follow best practices to prevent common issues
